{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5584) to create differential tests for `cmd/who`. The task requires creating `cmd/who/who_test.go` with differential tests comparing the Go `who` implementation against the `gwho` GNU reference binary. Tests must cover srd097-who requirements R2.1-R2.4 (display options) and R3.1-R3.3 (exit codes and SIGPIPE). Tests must skip gracefully when gwho is not installed, use LC_ALL=C, and use normalizers for session-dependent output.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gwho\")` with `t.Skip` for graceful skip\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct: `{ Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n   - `testutils.NormalizeFunc` = `func([]byte) []byte` for output normalization\n   - cgo-based utmpx access in the who implementation\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic output\n   - Binary name normalization via regex (pattern from users_test.go)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd097-who.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for what the tests must cover\n     - Key requirements: R1.1 (default listing), R1.2 (FILE arg), R1.3 (who am i), R1.4 (exit 1 on unreadable), R2.1 (-H heading), R2.2 (-u idle), R2.3 (-b boot), R2.4 (-q count), R3.1 (exit 0), R3.2 (exit 1 error), R3.3 (SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: -r (runlevel), -d (dead processes) on macOS\n\n   - `docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-11.1.yaml`\n     - Test suite spec with test cases: who_default, who_heading, who_boot\n     - All use LC_ALL=C env, expect exit_code 0\n\n   - `cmd/who/main.go` (312 lines, full implementation)\n     - Uses cgo with `#include <utmpx.h>`\n     - Flags: -H (heading), -u (idle), -b (boot), -q (count)\n     - Long flags: --heading, --users, --boot, --count, --help, --version\n     - \"who am i\" detection: when 2 remaining args, sets amI=true\n     - FILE argument: when 1 remaining arg, calls setUtmpxFile\n     - Error handling: exits 1 on unrecognized options and extra operands\n     - Key functions: parseArgs, readEntries, readBootTime, printHeader, printEntry, printCount, printBootEntry\n\n   - `cmd/users/users_test.go` (37 lines, pattern to follow)\n     - Pattern file for differential testing of utmpx utilities\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd096-users R2.1, R2.2, R2.3.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"os/exec\"\n         \"regexp\"\n         \"testing\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gusers\")\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n         }\n         binaryNameRe := regexp.MustCompile(`(?:/\\S+/)?g?users`)\n         normalizeBinaryName := testutils.NormalizeFunc(func(b []byte) []byte {\n             return binaryNameRe.ReplaceAll(b, []byte(\"users\"))\n         })\n         errNorm := []testutils.NormalizeFunc{normalizeBinaryName}\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n             {Name: \"no_args\", ExitCode: 0},\n             {Name: \"extra_operand\", Args: []string{\"/dev/null\", \"/dev/null\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n             {Name: \"unrecognized_option\", Args: []string{\"--foo\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n             {Name: \"invalid_short_option\", Args: []string{\"-x\"}, ExitCode: 1, Normalize: errNorm},\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/who/who_test.go` - FILE TO CREATE (not yet written)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - code has not been written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - No problems encountered yet. I read all four required files and was about to write the test file.\n   - Key consideration: who output is session-dependent (logged-in users, idle times, boot time all vary), so normalizers may be needed for timestamp fields. However, since differential testing compares both binaries on the same machine at the same time, outputs should match without normalization for most cases. Binary name normalization is needed for error messages.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive stitch task prompt with full project context, task description, SRDs, architecture docs, constitutions, and instructions to implement task #5584 - creating `cmd/who/who_test.go` with differential tests.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/who/who_test.go` with differential tests covering:\n     - Default output (no args) - traces R1.1, R3.1\n     - -H/--heading flag - traces R2.1\n     - -u/--users flag (idle time) - traces R2.2\n     - -b/--boot flag - traces R2.3\n     - -q/--count flag - traces R2.4\n     - Error cases (invalid option, extra operand) - traces R3.2\n     - Combined flags (e.g., -Hb, -Hu)\n     - Graceful skip when gwho not found - traces R4\n   - Verify compilation with `go vet ./cmd/who/`\n   - Run tests with `go test ./cmd/who/... -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four required files (srd097-who.yaml, test-rel-11.1.yaml, cmd/who/main.go, cmd/users/users_test.go) and was about to write `cmd/who/who_test.go`. I had all the context needed:\n   - The pattern from users_test.go (binary name normalizer, DiffTest slice structure)\n   - The SRD requirements to cover (R2.1-R2.4, R3.1-R3.3)\n   - The implementation details from main.go (flags, argument handling, error messages)\n   - The DiffTest struct signature from package_contracts\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/who/who_test.go` following the users_test.go pattern with:\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gwho\")` with t.Skip\n   - Binary name normalizer: `regexp.MustCompile(\"(?:/\\\\S+/)?g?who\")` replacing with \"who\"\n   - DiffTest cases: no_args (R1.1), heading -H (R2.1), idle -u (R2.2), boot -b (R2.3), count -q (R2.4), heading_and_boot -Hb, heading_and_users -Hu, error cases for invalid options (R3.2)\n   - Then verify with `go vet ./cmd/who/` and `go test ./cmd/who/... -count=1`\n\n   This is directly from the task description: \"Create TestDiff function using testutils.BuildBinary and testutils.RunDiffTests\" and \"Add DiffTest cases covering srd097-who R2.1-R2.4 behaviors\" and \"Add DiffTest cases covering srd097-who R3.1-R3.3 behaviors\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5584/bd50e5d8-0e52-4b70-978c-071471f3d08a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd50e5d8-0e52-4b70-978c-071471f3d08a","uuid":"e2927d80-2c05-4c43-bc32-01ffbdffe119","timestamp":"2026-05-27T14:31:16.467Z","isSynthetic":true}
